<title>USA: Jacksonville Bancorp gets ok for buyback.</title>
<headline>Jacksonville Bancorp gets ok for buyback.</headline>
<dateline>JACKSONVILLE, Texas 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jacksonville Bancorp Inc said Friday that the U.S. Office of Thrift Supervision has approved its program to repurchase up to five percent of its outstanding shares, or 127,073 shares, beginning April 24.</p>
<p>The company said it will buy the shares at prevailing market prices over a six month period, depending on market conditions.</p>
<p>It said the repurchased shares will become treasury shares available for general corporate purposes.</p>
<p>Jacksonville Bancorp is the holding company for Jacksonville Savings and Loan Association and Jacksonville I.H.C.</p>
</text>
